  "id": "COMPOUND:29853 - PROTEIN:5817",
  "verbalization": "The compound [(10R,11R,12R,13R,15R)-3,4,5,12,21,22,23-heptahydroxy-8,18-dioxo-13-(3,4,5-trihydroxybenzoyl)oxy-9,14,17-trioxatetracyclo[17.4.0.02,7.010,15]tricosa-1(23),2,4,6,19,21-hexaen-11-yl] 3,4,5-trihydroxybenzoate) is shown to target HepG2 through multiple pathways. It is directly linked to RXF 631, which in turn targets HepG2. Additionally, the compound is also linked to Raji, which targets Diosmetin 7-O-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-Beta-D-Glucopyranosyl-(1->2)-[Alpha-L-Rhamnopyranosyl-(1->6)]-Beta-D-Glucopyranoside, which also targets HepG2. These findings suggest that the compound may act as a broad-spectrum target for HepG2, possibly through a common mechanism involving the activation of cellular pathways or the inhibition of specific enzymes. The evidence supports a potential role for this compound in targeting HepG2, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
